'' fbc's OWN fbc-int/query-symbol.bas, with its suite runner, RUN. Three things kept it from
'' running: TKO0770 on the reserved name it queries; the reserved class answered 0; and,
'' in this Debug build, an abort in StmtCall_ (latesweeps4.bas), which took a STATEMENT
'' payload for every node and read past 'stmts' -- out of bounds once the index met the
'' vector's capacity. All 357 asserts pass since FB_SYMBCLASS_KEYWORD (line 84) and
'' FB_SYMBCLASS_FWDREF (line 116) are answered (afc9d179).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -m fbc-tests tests/vendor/fbc-tests/fbc-tests.bas tests/vendor/fbc-tests/fbc-int/query-symbol.bas -o tests/codegen/qsymvendor.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' ENV: TIKO_INCLUDE=toolchains/tiko-windows/inc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0770
'' RUN: tests/codegen/qsymvendor.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:      357       357         0  fbc_tests.fbc_int.query_symbol                 3
